tRefs":["DUTT-4-64-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4063006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"05daec461021e778b5079fe2b8ea12bd7b7ac9e17a38ade9df574f7fe93a3a8c","compact":"ef7cbef357b2e62e6da9f149c4738fa7d639a0e5ad12d2039be1b2e85be89e9a","nasal":"357735fa7893e3d25b9db47702d9d987053d1b7509bfca542b9f64efefd5dac4"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-63-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":63,"verse":7,"english":"Seeing the sea, here as if asleep, there, as if playful, and at another place with surges measuring mountains; and thronged with the foremost Dānavas inhabiting the nether regions; and capable of causing one's hair to stand on end, those powerful monkeys were seized with sadness.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-64-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4063007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1df221288f05fd79fb8f3b6e4f2e07db8648b3c84fb4be13f96e4730c6bde8fa","compact":"878ad68664936bd0d161631cfc7e3eb1e8c76a43e83d0b68e4343ad071b11f0c","nasal":"8c5141b832c1c11169e8ad914c184a97cdcbe09ffaf5826ff7dee99e59403574"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-63-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":63,"verse":8,"english":"Seeing the sea, incapable of being crossed even as the sky, all the monkeys began to lament, saying,-What is to be done?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-64-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4063008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e329da2e457fb01a76469530abf9789ba2d4393cbf90dca39c03752f4924c4f8","compact":"715a9289531e04a53edc385c8aec398b7701face57d0730b5fd14deda1a088ed","nasal":"715a9289531e04a53edc385c8aec398b7701face57d0730b5fd14deda1a088ed"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-63-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":63,"verse":9,"english":"That best of monkeys-(Angada), seeing the army cast down because of the sight of the sea, began to comfort the monkeys, afflicted with fear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-64-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4063009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"44a364ab4a9caecdb4c75b5ab2a5e57353a3a7f837366f9732f375419e6208da","compact":"5bf7202083be98f3d77f9c37013f0e869d811bbb8f2511d1249f66b19f1f2778","nasal":"e7a673b702d5fce10db941874c72f38b2fa5a91bdae3bbd234b32b91fbfaa12b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-63-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":63,"verse":10,"english":"We should not indulge in grief. Grief is injurious.-Grief destroys a person even as a wrathful serpent does a boy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.724,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-64-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4063010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"263dcefca12a3b0a1e6e42bfbf97efde003ac361dd796f5c3a40283a0604246a","compact":"53ab95797b9cf19ae00f422c3a217fea094b8ae21f976c084d0b3bfd839c59e7","nasal":"effa8ea1dbce4eacd56d917babd1d60ce50085441f213210ca7f710c6ef0838b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-63-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":63,"verse":11,"english":"He that, when the time is come for displaying his prowess, indulges in sorrow, growing weak in energy, fails to attain his objects.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.617,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-64-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4063011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"232197fb971a87331748999b13c503fc70ae1877a86b2fd145bec19fa56aa109","compact":"8de77caa63c655aa5136f2a8552f854053f72ab9f16b01782f012a061cb322c0","nasal":"8de77caa63c655aa5136f2a8552f854053f72ab9f16b01782f012a061cb322c0"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-63-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":63,"verse":12,"english":"That night having passed away, Angada in company with the monkeys, joined by the old ones, again took counsel with them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-64-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4063012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1da5765b905dba5dc6b4ec2ac1061cf9f1d418520d4189d5edfb352b6c49ec14","compact":"613b61869f39615b1104b4a719711d0e9510754e4a052c53b9116b3aaa9c8c5a","nasal":"b97ec77177979f7480fe7732f9e418e16443ed87d1c8b0a547eea697d5386405"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-63-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":63,"verse":13,"english":"That monkey-host surrounding Angada, resembled the host of Maruts environing Vasava.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.85,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-64-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4063013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"661fd9da973b5695f2936ab51b5248d9f5eb8bf0a717194027fcfcd6573279a7","compact":"9488762f8fc545c7c66a6db3d5e04e4735d6f2fdf871823cc64976cc74af13c2","nasal":"e7cb74f99c0bae3edd93dc57309754d665137abe7b6bca2c420f77ca42410a67"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-63-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":63,"verse":14,"english":"Who save Väli's son (stationed) at one place and at another Hanumān, could be capable of stilling that force?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.766,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-64-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4063014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"964a0767c54b108a2fa067aa2b854782fc3276b31053cf83f1f0e9cd40c8cf58","compact":"faa53f9f09185113c955580033ee281aabd8f564e33e80f